  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-09T06:53:59.211Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When you select another player, the icon above \"Clone Avatar\" in the Quick Menu indicates whether the avatar they are wearing is PC/Quest built or not.\nHowever, currently it is not showing correctly and is instead showing the icon for \"my current platform\".\nThus, when you are playing on PCVR on Steam, all the avatars of the players around you represent the so-called \"PC-only\" avatars.\nFor example, in the attached image, the well-known officially Public Avatar \"kamilaquest\" is displayed as if it were a \"PC-only\" avatar. (Of course, it is a cross-platform avatar, and the person of the image is a Quest player to begin with.)\nThis has been occurring on both PC and Quest since about 2022/04/08 in both RELEASE and BETA TEST.\nRelated to this problem, the following issues (canny have already been resolved) is occurring at the same time, \n( https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/problem-with-avatars )\nSince this was a server problem, it is assumed that this problem is similar.\nNot only does this issue prevent players from knowing which platform avatars were built on, but it also prevents them from knowing if public avatars can really be cloned in the platform they are playing on.",
